{
  "_comment": [
    "The DNP3 object catalog of go-dnp3: every group and variation the app package encodes and decodes, from IEEE 1815-2012 Annex A.",
    "It is the source of truth: `go generate ./...` (internal/cmd/gencatalog) writes app/registry_table.go, client/points_table.go and OBJECTS.md from it; CI fails when they drift.",
    "family is the codec of the app package that encodes the variation; number the width of its value; time absolute (48-bit) or relative (16-bit, after a CTO); size the octets of one object, null when not fixed; point marks data that client.Measurements reports.",
    "openGroups are the groups whose variation is not a fixed set (device attributes; octet strings, whose variation is the length): the app package handles them in code."
  ],
  "standard": "IEEE 1815-2012 Annex A",
